    {
      "id": "claim_6e8bfcd388334587a29d3d9118ce0a4f",
      "statement": "On each gated validation epoch the monitor executes a fixed sequence: it gates on epoch % every_n_epochs == 0 (rank-symmetric values only), resolves the paired dataset lazily as getattr(source, \"val_latent_ds\", source) so the cold path's post-setup replacement is honored, selects and caches a seeded randperm prefix of subset_size subjects collated with default_collate, draws freshly seeded start noise on the module's device and dtype, runs the module's own full Heun sample() rollout under torch.inference_mode, decodes the generated and real target latents through VaeStage plus LatentDecoder, normalizes both volumes with min_max_to_unit, scores them with PairedFidelityMetrics, and logs val/psnr and val/ssim through two module-attached torchmetrics MeanMetrics that are reset each epoch so the logged value is the current epoch's rather than an accumulation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired_callback.py#L112-L215",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6156b1725d9f333f8bd20ae53685fe89dcf215c6759729b8928ee8ab5aa0f572:"
        },
        {
